---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';import Visual from '../components/Visual.astro';import ToolCard from '../components/ToolCard.astro';import {getCollection} from 'astro:content';
import { catalogueSchema } from '../lib';
const tools=await getCollection('tools');const find=(id:string)=>tools.find(t=>t.id===id)!;
---
<Base structuredData={[catalogueSchema('TradingView indicators', tools.filter(t=>t.data.group==='indicator'), Astro.url.pathname, Astro.site!)]} title="TradingView indicators for CFD charts" description="Pine indicators for CFD trading in TradingView. Connect CFD tickers to exchange symbols for company information, volume and percentage levels.">
<section class="section-shell page-intro"><div class="eyebrow">INDICATORS / TRADINGVIEW PINE</div><h1>Your CFD chart.<br/><span>The underlying context.</span></h1><p class="lead">When you view a stock CFD, these indicators can show data for the matching stock symbol listed on Nasdaq or the NYSE. With the symbol mapping set up, they select that exchange symbol automatically and display its company information or volume beside your CFD chart. Index CFDs use suitable futures and ETFs for percentage levels and a volume activity proxy.</p><div class="jump-links"><a href="#setup">Start here ↘</a><a href="#stocks">Stocks ↘</a><a href="#indices">Indices ↘</a></div></section>
<section class="section-shell"><p class="device-note">Read on mobile, set up on desktop. These indicators are designed around the author’s desktop workflow. TradingView mobile can render Pine, but their mobile output has not been reviewed or tested by the author.</p></section>
<section id="setup" class="section-shell setup-feature"><div><div class="eyebrow">START HERE / SHARED SETUP</div><h2>Set up shared<br/>symbol mapping.</h2><p>Symbol Mapper matches a broker CFD ticker to its exchange symbol. Add it to the chart and connect both code inputs in each indicator that needs it.</p><p class="muted">It stays visually silent. Keep it on the chart while those inputs are used. A suitable local mapping or explicit volume formula takes priority, so Mapper is not always required.</p><a href="/tools/symbol-mapper/" class="button primary">Set up Symbol Mapper <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><Visual kind="mapper" diagram={find("symbol-mapper").data.diagram}/></section>
<section id="stocks" class="section-shell section-space"><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">01 / STOCKS</div><h2>Company information<br/>and stock volume.</h2></div><p>See the company behind a stock CFD and choose its exchange volume. Source coverage and broker mappings still matter.</p></div><div class="tool-grid two"><ToolCard tool={find('info')}/><ToolCard tool={find('real-volume')}/></div></section>
<section id="indices" class="section-shell section-space border-top"><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">02 / INDICES</div><h2>Index CFD levels<br/>and volume proxies.</h2></div><p>Levels focuses on Nasdaq 100 and S&P 500 CFDs. Real Volume combines defined futures and ETF sources into an activity proxy.</p></div><div class="tool-grid two"><ToolCard tool={find('cfd-levels')}/><ToolCard tool={find('real-volume')} volumeMarket="indices"/></div><p class="section-footnote">Real Volume is the same tool in both sections. Indices do not have directly traded volume. IG and Trade Nation mappings are configuration specific, not universal broker support.</p></section>
</Base>
